  "title": "Pairs collapse the cyclic action to an involution and triples decide: counting maps to nilpotent-by-cyclic groups at every sector order",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "For p-groups of exponent p with a coprime cyclic action, counting maps from closed 3-manifolds with H1(M; F_p) = 0 is polynomial at a sector order whenever nontrivial characters bracket only with their inverses, collapsing the action to an involution, and that involution's Lie triple system is abelian; for graded class at most 4 it is #P-hard when pairs hold and a triple survives, at every sector order. Pair failures in classes 3-4 remain open.",
